blocks.explanation:
All callbacks close over the same function-scoped `i` binding. The timer callbacks run after the loop has completed, at which point `i` is `3`.

Using `let` creates a new binding for each loop iteration:

```javascript
for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 0);
}
// 0, 1, 2
```

